{
  // Most technologies are double-edged: a tree of pure upgrades would quietly teach that
  // centralization is free. "Local" effects (production, defense, goods upkeep, political
  // education) apply to communes that hold the tech; everything else scales with the share
  // of the federation that holds it.
  //
  // Five lines of development, each in chains of two to four steps. Every line has an
  // efficient path that adds drift and a free path that brakes it at some cost, so growing
  // a line is a choice: a commune on a line's free path is reluctant to take up that line's
  // centralizing technologies (Balance.PathResistance). Communes discover what their education, needs and values lead them
  // to; the movement can only circulate ideas.
  "technologies": [

